WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:08.626
Punctuation changes what a sentence means.

2
00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:14.526
Oh no! This sounds like we are eating Grandma!

3
00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:20.101
One comma, and now we are talking TO Grandma.

4
00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:22.958
Punctuation saves lives!

5
00:00:24.933 --> 00:00:27.394
Every sentence ends with a mark.

6
00:00:30.367 --> 00:00:32.921
Full stop: it tells you something.

7
00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:38.176
Question mark: it asks something.

8
00:00:41.167 --> 00:00:44.278
Exclamation mark: surprise or strong feeling.

9
00:00:45.267 --> 00:00:48.425
Don't forget: a capital letter at the start!

10
00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:52.629
Commas separate items in a list.

11
00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:57.225
This list is hard to read.

12
00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:03.068
Put a comma between each item.

13
00:01:05.067 --> 00:01:07.853
Use 'and' before the last item instead.

14
00:01:09.833 --> 00:01:11.598
Apostrophes have two jobs.

15
00:01:12.567 --> 00:01:15.214
Job 1: show where letters are missing.

16
00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:24.265
The 'o' goes. The apostrophe takes its place.

17
00:01:35.233 --> 00:01:38.577
I am becomes I'm. It is becomes it's.

18
00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:43.864
Job 2: show that something belongs to someone.

19
00:01:46.833 --> 00:01:48.876
The bone belongs to the dog.

20
00:01:52.867 --> 00:01:56.443
Write the owner, then apostrophe s: the dog's bone.

21
00:01:59.433 --> 00:02:03.055
More than one owner ending in s? Apostrophe after the s.

22
00:02:05.033 --> 00:02:08.284
Speech marks show the exact words someone says.

23
00:02:11.267 --> 00:02:13.171
Sam says: I am hungry!

24
00:02:17.667 --> 00:02:20.361
The spoken words go inside the speech marks.

25
00:02:22.333 --> 00:02:24.701
The ! goes inside the speech marks too.

26
00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:29.811
Your turn! Fix this sentence. Pause the video.

27
00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:40.636
Let's check.

28
00:02:41.633 --> 00:02:42.422
Capital I.

29
00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:46.501
Apostrophe: can't equals cannot.

30
00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.858
Names need a capital: Tom.

31
00:02:51.333 --> 00:02:54.027
Apostrophe: the bag belongs to Tom.

32
00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:57.125
Full stop at the end.

33
00:02:58.100 --> 00:02:59.679
How many did you spot?

34
00:03:06.167 --> 00:03:07.885
Little marks, big jobs!
